# Security headers for every route, in the Netlify/Cloudflare Pages format.
# Gatsby copies this file from static/ into the publish directory, and
# gatsby-node.js then rewrites the CSP placeholder below. Any host that does
# not read a _headers file must replicate the *rewritten* headers from
# public/_headers in its own configuration; see docs/RELEASE.md.
#
# Notes on the CSP.
#
# script-src carries no 'unsafe-inline'. Gatsby emits a small, fixed set of
# inline bootstrap scripts (the page path, the chunk mapping, the compilation
# hash), so they are allowlisted by SHA-256 instead. Those hashes change on
# every build, so the placeholder token in script-src below is substituted at
# build time rather than written out here; onPostBuild fails the build if that
# token is missing, so this cannot silently regress to a policy that allows
# arbitrary inline script. A browser ignores 'unsafe-inline' whenever a hash
# or nonce is present anyway, so the two cannot be combined as a fallback.
#
# style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline': styled-components injects rules through the
# CSSOM at runtime, which no hash can cover. That is a far weaker exposure
# than inline script and is accepted.
#
# Everything else is locked to 'self': the site talks to MetaMask through the
# injected provider, not the network, so no remote connect-src is needed.
# frame-ancestors 'none' (with the X-Frame-Options fallback) prevents the dapp
# from being framed for clickjacking a user's snap interactions.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' {{INLINE_SCRIPT_HASHES}}; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
